# PIN (`todo/t0953`, R50 Track E) — the DICT arm of the builtin-HOF
# closure-argument env drain. LIVE, not a gap: this fixture is expected to run
# ASan-CLEAN at HEAD and to go RED if the dict drain is reverted.
#
# WHY IT LIVES IN `known_gaps/` DESPITE BEING GREEN. The directory is an `OUT`
# row of `tests/sanitize/CORPUS_MANIFEST.txt` and is out of
# `runtime_parity_corpus`, so a fixture here costs no sanitize-corpus row and
# owes no same-round self-host parity port. `assert_gg_sanitize_clean` takes a
# subdirectory stem, so the ASan gate is fully live from here. A top-level
# `*.gg` would buy nothing and cost both.
#
# WHY THE ENCLOSING LOOP IS MANDATORY, NOT DECORATION. Per-element
# misplacement is already excluded — a single fold over two entries mints ONE
# temp regardless. What a one-trip fixture CANNOT see is a drain hoisted from
# per-CALL to per-FUNCTION: under a shared per-function ledger an N-trip loop
# leaks N-1 records and a 1-trip fixture is green. Twenty trips, one record
# per trip if the drain regresses.
#
# HEAP-FORCED: the closure CAPTURES `base`, so its environment is a real
# `__gorget_closure_env_alloc` block rather than an 8-byte placeholder, and
# LeakSanitizer sees it under the sweep's conservative-root setting.
#
# NOT A SECOND FILING: `todo/t0953` owns the class and stays OPEN on its
# plain-call cell. This pins the DICT expander cell that Track E closed.
#
# INTENDED: prints `5100` and runs ASan-CLEAN. Per trip the fold sums
# 30 + 100 and 25 + 100 = 255; twenty trips = 5100.
from std.collections import Dict

void main():
    Dict[String, int] ages = Dict[String, int]()
    ages.put("alice", 30)
    ages.put("bob", 25)
    int base = 100
    int total = 0
    int i = 0
    while i < 20:
        int sum = ages.fold(0, (int acc, String k, int v): acc + v + base)
        total = total + sum
        i = i + 1
    print(total)
